PRIVY_APP_ID=your-privy-app-id-here
MONGO_ROOT_USERNAME=duelme
MONGO_ROOT_PASSWORD=change-me-to-a-strong-password

# -- Dev-only testnet faucet ---------------------------------------------------
# The /api/v1/faucet/claim endpoint sends 0.001 ETH + 100 MockUSDT from
# FAUCET_PRIVATE_KEY to any authenticated user, once per wallet. Enable only on
# dev hosts. Production compose hardcodes `FAUCET_ENABLED=false` as a
# defense-in-depth kill switch — do NOT remove that hardcoded value from
# ops/docker-compose.prod.yml.
#
# SECURITY: use a DEDICATED hot wallet. Never reuse a key that holds mainnet
# funds — if the dev host is compromised, the key is gone.
#FAUCET_ENABLED=true
#FAUCET_PRIVATE_KEY=your-dev-hot-wallet-private-key-hex

# -- Gasless relaying (ERC-2771) -----------------------------------------------
# The frontend's /api/relay signs and pays for a player's duel action so they never
# need ETH. CI writes all four of these into the server .env on every deploy; the two
# budget lines have no secret behind them and land empty, which is deliberate — the
# code defaults in frontend/src/lib/relayerConfig.ts then apply (0.0005 ETH per address
# per day, 0.01 ETH across all of them).
#
# Leave RELAYER_PRIVATE_KEY unset and nothing breaks: /api/relay answers 503 and duel
# writes stay self-paid by the player. That is the fallback, not an outage.
#
# Relaying also needs a forwarder recorded for the build's default chain in
# frontend/src/lib/constants.ts — an unset `forwarder` disables it just as surely as a
# missing key, and the reason reads "No ERC-2771 forwarder recorded for chain N".
#
# SECURITY: a DEDICATED hot wallet per environment, funded with only what the daily
# budgets can spend. It signs nothing but ERC2771Forwarder.execute, but a compromised
# host still drains whatever sits in it. Never point dev and prod at the same key.
#RELAYER_PRIVATE_KEY=your-dedicated-relayer-hot-wallet-private-key-hex
# Server-side RPC. A browser-locked NEXT_PUBLIC_ key is rejected here, because a server
# request sends no Origin header. Falls back to the chain's public RPC when unset.
#RELAYER_RPC_URL=https://arb1.arbitrum.io/rpc
#RELAYER_DAILY_BUDGET_WEI=500000000000000
#RELAYER_GLOBAL_DAILY_BUDGET_WEI=10000000000000000
